Hi,<br><br>- Physics for game programmers by Grant Palmer<br>Accessible and not too complex<br><br>- Physics For Dummies by Steve Holzner<br>Not kidding, it's pretty good to get your head around some concepts in physics or refresh your memory.<br><br>- Real-time collision detection by Christer Ericson<br>Everything you need to know about collision detection<br><br>- Physics based animation by Kenny Erleben, Jon Sporring, Knud Henriksen and Henrik Dohlmann<br>Really advanced, I would not recommend this for a beginner<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8961">Vince01</a> — Wed Dec 14, 2011 6:15 pm</p><hr />
